1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:02,510
This engineer's candy bar melted in his

2
00:00:02,510 --> 00:00:05,010
pocket... and nothing near him was hot.

3
00:00:05,370 --> 00:00:06,150
It was 1945.

4
00:00:07,030 --> 00:00:09,310
Percy Spencer was building magnetrons, the

5
00:00:09,310 --> 00:00:10,900
glowing tubes that power radar.

6
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:13,400
So the story goes, he aimed one at

7
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:15,320
popcorn. It popped.

8
00:00:16,060 --> 00:00:16,840
Then at an egg.

9
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:18,430
It exploded.

10
00:00:18,730 --> 00:00:20,950
The invisible waves were shaking the water

11
00:00:20,950 --> 00:00:21,870
inside the food.

12
00:00:22,470 --> 00:00:24,560
And all that shaking made heat.

13
00:00:24,860 --> 00:00:27,340
The first microwave oven, in 1947, was

14
00:00:27,340 --> 00:00:29,700
almost six feet tall, and weighed about

15
00:00:29,700 --> 00:00:31,490
seven hundred and fifty pounds.

16
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:34,300
So next time you warm up your food...

17
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:34,960
check your pockets.
